  "decisionBasis": {
    "confirmed": [
      "The actual WebGL Bellows renderable contributes to the canvas drawing buffer in two selected drawElements calls under observed source-over RGB blending.",
      "Same-material isolated B0 replays are repeatable on WebGL and native material-aware WebGPU; at five common covered samples their RGBA32F representation-matched proxy difference is small.",
      "B3 remains a small improvement against the much larger four-state dimmed-response residual."
    ],
    "unresolved": [
      "The dominant native residual cannot be decomposed among source, destination, and blend stages because the original native draw boundary is not publicly readable in Three r186.",
      "F2 replay alters visibility, depth context, draw order, and blending, so it is not an unchanged production fragment."
    ],
    "promotionBoundary": "Anatomy remains M2 \u2014 OPT-IN IMPLEMENTATION INCOMPLETE. No PR N, default output correction, WebGPU promotion, or production change is authorized."
  },
